<StaticPage title="Editorial principles" deck="The standards OGCTV intends to apply to reporting, editing and corrections." eyebrow="Standards" updated="6 October 2026"><h2>Accuracy before speed</h2><p>We seek to verify names, dates, locations, documents, images and material claims before publication. Breaking-news labels should be reserved for urgent, verified developments. Where facts are still emerging, we say what is known, what is not known and how the information was obtained.</p><h2>Fairness and right of reply</h2><p>People and institutions facing significant criticism should have a meaningful opportunity to respond. Allegations remain allegations unless established by reliable evidence or a competent legal process.</p><h2>Independence</h2><p>News coverage should not be shaped by political, commercial or personal interests. Advertising and sponsored material, if introduced, must be clearly distinguished from editorial work.</p><h2>Attribution and transparency</h2><p>We identify sources wherever it is safe and responsible to do so, explain anonymous sourcing when it is necessary, label opinion, and distinguish analysis from reporting. Artificial or illustrative images must not be presented as documentary evidence.</p><h2>Privacy and harm</h2><p>We balance the public interest against avoidable harm, especially when reporting on children, victims, grieving families and people in vulnerable situations.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Substantive errors should be corrected promptly and transparently. Readers can submit a correction request through the newsroom WhatsApp line.</p></StaticPage>
